## Key Concepts Explained

### 1. Remote Functions
```clubatime/src/lib/auth.remote.ts#L5-10
export const getSession = query(
  async () =>
    await auth.api.getSession({
      headers: getRequestEvent().request.headers,
    }),
);
```
- `query()` = for reading data (GET-like)
- `form()` = for actions/mutations (POST-like)
- They run on the server but can be called from components
- Works without JavaScript!

### 2. Using Remote Functions in Components
```/dev/null/example.svelte#L1-10
{#await getSession()}
  <p>Loading...</p>
{:then session}
  {#if session?.user}
    <p>Hello {session.user.name}</p>
  {:else}
    <p>Not signed in</p>
  {/if}
{/await}
```

### 3. Form Actions with Remote Functions
```/dev/null/example.svelte#L1-5
<form {...signIn}>
  <button type="submit">Sign In</button>
</form>
```
- `{...signIn}` spreads the form attributes (action, method)
- Works as a regular HTML form (no JS needed)
- Progressively enhanced when JS is available

### 4. Scoped CSS
Every `<style>` block in Svelte is **automatically scoped** to that component. You don't need to do anything special - classes won't leak to other components.

### 5. Dark Mode
Your CSS already defaults to dark mode via:
```clubatime/src/lib/styles/app.css#L31
color-scheme: dark;
```

