- Deploying one app (SvelteKit) is simpler than deploying a separate Rails service and maintaining cross-service auth.

When Ruby might make sense
- If your team already owns a mature Rails backend and prefers Ruby for server-side business logic, or you have Ruby infra/ops expertise.
- If you want to use Rails-specific features (very opinionated ActiveRecord patterns, lots of community gems for admin UIs) and accept the integration cost.

