- You’ll need to build and deploy a separate API (and host sessions/tokens) and wire your SvelteKit frontend to it (CORS, cookies, session syncing).
- You lose the convenience of SvelteKit remoteFunctions and server-only modules — you’ll call fetch to an external API instead of calling `query()` / `form()` that run on the same server.
- More infra overhead (two apps instead of one).

